{"id": "EUVD-2026-83388", "enisaUuid": "9e3159a8-24b1-3c77-8b5f-6f9094dfe3c3", "description": "Suricata is a network Intrusion Detection System, Intrusion Prevention System and Network Security Monitoring engine. From 7.0.0 until 7.0.17 and 8.0.6, the MQTT parser in rust/src/mqtt/mqtt.rs permits repeated PUBREC or PUBREL messages to be appended to one transaction without a limit. Crafted MQTT traffic can grow transaction state indefinitely, consuming CPU and memory and causing slowdown or denial of service. This issue is fixed in versions 8.0.6 and 7.0.17.", "datePublished": "2026-09-18T20:14:55", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-22T15:47:38", "baseScore": 7.5, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H", "references": ["https://github.com/OISF/suricata/security/advisories/GHSA-7h2h-hpj2-9w6p", "https://github.com/OISF/suricata/commit/03ba8a71d827dd36a0ceb512f45d2f440f260a3a", "https://github.com/OISF/suricata/commit/5cde93dea38533c9b225128ba9d54955997dc273", "https://github.com/OISF/suricata/commit/c03666d261256df5a2d1f5800872da8a5addf6a5", "https://github.com/OISF/suricata/releases/tag/suricata-7.0.17", "https://github.com/OISF/suricata/releases/tag/suricata-8.0.6", "https://redmine.openinfosecfoundation.org/issues/8525"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-57227"], "assigner": "GitHub_M", "epss": 0.7, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "6a8c81c8-c2de-3789-8870-6ad44df0deab", "product": {"name": "suricata", "vendor": {"name": "OISF"}}, "product_version": "8.0.0, < 8.0.6"}, {"id": "809969ef-8cef-3c42-8213-3ca846900847", "product": {"name": "suricata", "vendor": {"name": "OISF"}}, "product_version": "7.0.0, < 7.0.17"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "ac329acf-2a5a-391e-95a1-6d7d3a45cce4", "vendor": {"name": "OISF"}}], "isExploited": false}